---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { photos } from "../data/site";
---

<Base
  title="Our Story – AWKN® Korean Apothecary"
  description="Tess and Soom, the sisters behind AWKN, and the year of research that became Night Owl."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="kicker">Our story</p>
    <h1>Meet the sisters behind AWKN.</h1>
  </header>
  <section class="story-grid">
    <img src={photos.storyArt} alt="Illustrated portrait of the AWKN sisters" data-seat="mast" data-seat-edge="inside" />
    <div class="narrow">
      <p>
        We took a first step to address something that was a real issue in our lives, and to bring something personal from our culture and heritage. After a year of research and preparation, we launched AWKN.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is important that we share that journey, and invite you to be part of it. From our family to yours.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="pair">
      <article>
        <img src={photos.tess} alt="Tess, co-founder of AWKN" data-seat="founder" data-seat-edge="inside" />
        <h3>Tess</h3>
        <p>
          During a career in tech and start-ups, Tess kept balancing high-performance workdays with social nights. That is what made her want to share Korea’s recovery rituals, the ones traditionally used before and after a celebration.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <img src={photos.soom} alt="Soom, co-founder of AWKN" data-seat="founder" data-seat-edge="inside" />
        <h3>Soom</h3>
        <p>
          For years Soom held back at gatherings because of a sensitivity many people of East Asian descent know as Asian flush. AWKN became a personal ritual for staying in the celebration.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
